<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Protection Warrior Tank in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel and Trial of the Crusader raids. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, BoE World drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h2>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> is a big step up to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> when it comes to damage dealt to tanks and difficulty in general. Several bosses in <b>heroic</b> difficulty top <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> in sustained damage output and add tank-buster abilities on top that can one-shot a geared tank without proper planning of defensive cooldowns. Thankfully, the ilvl 264 and ilvl 277 upgrades are just as big of a step up compared to the last phase, with a much-needed 26% increase in survivability between P3 BiS and P4 BiS. However, tank survival before a few upgrades is going to be a challenge and the main difficulty for many encounters in the early weeks of Phase 4. For this reason, it is highly recommended to run the 10-man version of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> to gather potential upgrades before attempting the more challenging encounters of the 25-man version.<br/>
<br/>
<i>Keep in mind that gearing your <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> highly depends on your raiding environment. While I may recommend mostly defensive gear sets that will fit the majority of players, only you can know what kind of threat is needed in your raid. If your guild requires a <i>higher threat ceiling</i> to withstand the pressure from high-performing damage dealers, then feel free to mix in threat-oriented items to find the <b>balance</b> between threat and survival that works best for <i>your</i> group. But first, make sure your rotation is on point with this <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/warrior/protection/tank-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve">Rotation and Cooldowns guide</a>!</i>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-question">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>How good is the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-260/sanctified-ymirjar-lords-plate">Protection Warrior Tier 10 set</a>?</b></div></li>
<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">2 pieces: <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70843">Your Shield Slam and Shockwave abilities deal 20% increased damage.</a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">4 pieces: <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70844">Your Bloodrage ability no longer costs health to use, and now causes you to absorb damage equal to 20% of your maximum health.  Lasts until cancelled.</a></div></li></ul>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">The Tier 10 2-piece set bonus is a +4.5% DPS and +5% TPS increase roughly, which brings additional threat all the while still wearing mitigation-focused items. Most parts of the T10 set are BiS for their respective slot so this set bonus is the cherry on top.<br/>
<br/>The <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70844">4-piece bonus</a> turns <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=2687/bloodrage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_bloodrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodrage</span></a> into an additional minor defensive cooldown that creates an absorption shield equal to 20% of your maximum health (about 11.7k HP absorb in P4 BiS) on top of generating rage. This absorption shield lasts until depleted or until the 10-second effect of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=2687/bloodrage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_bloodrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodrage</span></a> runs out. A useful set bonus that lets you buffer your healthpool every minute to help mitigate a big tank-buster ability or adds another emergency cooldown to your toolkit.<br/>Unfortunately, the <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/warrior">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a>'s set bonus isn't as potent as the stronger <span class="c11">Feral</span> <a class="icontiny c11" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/druid">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_druid.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Druid</span></a> <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70726">4-piece bonus</a> and <span class="c6">Blood</span> <a class="icontiny c6" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/death-knight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a> <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70652">4-piece bonus</a>, which both provide 12% damage reduction for a full 10 seconds every minute. But this time, <span class="c2">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c2" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/paladin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_paladin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Paladin</span></a>
<span class="c2">s</span> got the short end of the stick, with a set bonus that provides <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70761">12% dodge for 10 sec</a> and will do nothing against most unavoidable tank-buster abilities.</div></li></ul>
