<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Triumph for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49426/emblem-of-frost">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></a> drop from the <b>10-man and 25-man</b> <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> bosses and can be exchanged for gear in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4395/dalaran">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dalaran</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>Unlike the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-162">Tier 9</a> that was replaced with each new version, each piece of the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-852">Tier 10</a> set can be upgraded, from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-852">ilvl 251</a> to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-241">ilvl 264</a> and to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-260">ilvl 277</a> using their previous version, paired with a <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52026/protectors-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Protector's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> and <b>heroic</b> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52029/protectors-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Protector's Mark of Sanctification</span></a>. This means you will have to buy the base <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-852">ilvl 251 version</a> of your T10 set with your <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> to ultimately wear the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-260">ilvl 277 version</a>.<br/>
<br/>However, the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67273">T9 4-piece set bonus</a> is so strong that it is not worth replacing your <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-200">ilvl 258 T9</a> or <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-162">ilvl 245 T9</a> items until you have at least upgraded 4 parts of your T10 to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-241">ilvl 264</a>, or 2 parts to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-241">ilvl 264</a> + 2 parts <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-852">ilvl 251</a> + <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49904/pillars-of-might">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pillars of Might</span></a> or any ilvl 277 off-set you may have received early from one of the easy <b>heroic</b> bosses.<br/>Since it will take a few weeks to amass 310-345 <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> and buy 4 pieces of your <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-852">ilvl 251 T10</a>, plus upgrade them with 2-4 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52026/protectors-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Protector's Mark of Sanctification</span></a>, my recommendation is to wait until the last moment before buying any parts. Throughout these few weeks of raiding <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=38433/toravon-the-ice-watcher">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Toravon the Ice Watcher</span></a>, chances are you will receive several ilvl 264 or ilvl 277 upgrades that will affect which 4 parts of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-241">T10</a> you ultimately want to build around what you already have.<br/>
<br/>Assuming you don't have a single upgrade from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> that would affect your choice of T10 items, the biggest upgrades compared to a baseline of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=-200">ilvl 258 Tier 9</a> are <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51217">gloves</a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51219">chest</a> — for their bonus armor — followed by <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51215">shoulders</a>, while <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51216">legs</a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51218">helm</a> are the lowest upgrades.<br/>Since <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49904/pillars-of-might">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pillars of Might</span></a> are an amazing item that you can craft week 1 of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>, a guaranteed upgrade path without relying on any lucky raid drop would be to use <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51218">helm</a> + <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51215">shoulders</a> + <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51219">chest</a> + <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51217">gloves</a> for the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70844">T10 4-piece bonus</a>, paired with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49904/pillars-of-might">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pillars of Might</span></a> as your off-set. However, you will want to ultimately upgrade the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51216">T10 legs</a> as well to branch out to the end-game BiS which uses the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50640/broken-ram-skull-helm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_151.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Broken Ram Skull Helm</span></a> helmet as the off-set slot, instead of legs. <br/>
<br/>Besides the different T10 parts, none of the items you can purchase with your <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> are BiS per se. <br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50466/sentinels-winter-cloak">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sentinel's Winter Cloak</span></a> is a good catch-up cloak, on par with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47549/magnis-resolution">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Magni's Resolution</span></a> if you have been unlucky so far or didn't manage to complete a 50 attempt tribute.<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50991/verdigris-chain-belt">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Verdigris Chain Belt</span></a> is the second-best belt in Phase 4 behind the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50691/belt-of-broken-bones">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_63.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of Broken Bones</span></a>. A worthy investment if your group struggles to defeat <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36626/festergut">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Festergut</span></a> in <b>heroic</b> difficulty.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a>, while it may look tempting based on the stamina it provides, performs worse than most Phase 3 trinkets due to a mediocre <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71586">on-use effect</a> so it's definitely not something to rush buying, unless your trinket alternatives are very poor. Refer to the trinkets section of this guide for more details.<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50968/cataclysmic-chestguard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_25.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cataclysmic Chestguard</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50978/gauntlets-of-the-kraken">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_86.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of the Kraken</span></a>, while good standalone items thanks to bonus armor, are just sidegrades to your ilvl 264 <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51219">chest</a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51217">gloves</a> so ultimately wasted <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a>.<br/>
