<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="wrist">Wrist for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h3>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50611/bracers-of-dark-reckoning">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_43.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bracers of Dark Reckoning</span></a> and the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51901/gargoyle-spit-bracers">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_43.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gargoyle Spit Bracers</span></a> are neck and neck in simulations and EHP, with only a slight edge for the ilvl 277 due to their superior item budget and stamina. This goes to show how valuable bonus armor is, with a lower item level item competing for best simply due to better budget allocation. <br/>Their normal versions <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49960/bracers-of-dark-reckoning">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_42.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bracers of Dark Reckoning</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50802/gargoyle-spit-bracers">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_42.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gargoyle Spit Bracers</span></a> are only minor upgrades to Phase 3 BiS <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47111/bracers-of-the-shieldmaiden">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_31.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bracers of the Shieldmaiden</span></a>. However, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47111/bracers-of-the-shieldmaiden">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_31.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bracers of the Shieldmaiden</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47918/dreadscale-armguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dreadscale Armguards</span></a> remain relevant in Phase 4 as the best bracers with expertise and hit rating respectively, should you need the stats in a more offensive gear set.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Bracer Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=62256/enchant-bracers-major-stamina">
