<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="waist">Waist for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h3>Similarly to wrists, few belts are added to this phase. The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50691/belt-of-broken-bones">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_63.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of Broken Bones</span></a> is the only ilvl 277 belt in Phase 4 and therefore BiS by default due to its superior item budget and stamina. On the bright side, it drops from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36626/festergut">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Festergut</span></a>, one of the easiest heroic encounters, so it should be reasonably easy to get. <br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50991/verdigris-chain-belt">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Verdigris Chain Belt</span></a> is a close second despite its lower item level, once again thanks to bonus armor. The main downside is that it costs <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=341/emblem-of-frost">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></span></a> so you might want to consider purchasing it only after buying your entire T10 set, at which point you may already have the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50691/belt-of-broken-bones">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_63.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of Broken Bones</span></a>. Consider it a consolation prize if you have yet to see the ilvl 277 belt drop after a few weeks.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51831/ironrope-belt-of-ymirjar">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_63.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ironrope Belt of Ymirjar</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50036/belt-of-broken-bones">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Belt of Broken Bones</span></a> are only small upgrades to Phase 3 BiS <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47076/girdle-of-bloodied-scars">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_48c.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Girdle of Bloodied Scars</span></a>, although the former is still worth grabbing in case you need additional hit rating for a balanced/<wbr/>threat-oriented set. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Waist Enchant</b>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41611/eternal-belt-buckle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_36.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Eternal Belt Buckle</span></a>
