<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="legs">Legs for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h3>The ilvl 277 T10 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51223/sanctified-ymirjar-lords-legguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Ymirjar Lord's Legguards</span></a> are the best legs thanks to an excellent stats distribution and a no-brainer to activate your <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70844">4-piece set bonus</a>. However, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50612/legguards-of-lost-hope">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_31.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legguards of Lost Hope</span></a> are a close second, with hit rating in place of expertise, and drop from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36612/lord-marrowgar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lord Marrowgar</span></a>, one of the easiest heroic bosses. They are definitely worth considering if you get them early, should you buy different T10 pieces to activate the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70844">4-piece set bonus</a> around it.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49904/pillars-of-might">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pillars of Might</span></a> are a relatively affordable <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70567">craft</a> available to Blacksmiths once Revered with <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/faction=1156/the-ashen-verdict">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Ashen Verdict</span></a>. These ilvl 264 legs are the best mitigation legs for the rest of the game thanks to their bonus armor and a big upgrade to your Phase 3 BiS <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48447/wrynns-legguards-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_24.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wrynn's Legguards of Triumph</span></a> that can be crafted week 1 of Phase 4. I recommend crafting and equipping them as soon as possible as they will greatly help your progression in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>, assuming you have at least an ilvl 245 T9 chest <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48450/wrynns-breastplate-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_25.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wrynn's Breastplate of Triumph</span></a> to maintain the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67273">4-piece T9 set bonus</a>. They will also make equipping your <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70844">4-piece T10 set bonus</a> worth it as early as you can upgrade the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51219">chest</a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51217">gloves</a> to ilvl 264.<br/>
<br/>The ilvl 264 T10 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51216/sanctified-ymirjar-lords-legguards">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctified Ymirjar Lord's Legguards</span></a> pale in comparison to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49904/pillars-of-might">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_32.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pillars of Might</span></a> and are only worth using to activate the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70844">4-piece T10 set bonus</a> if you already have a superior ilvl 277 item as your off-set, in the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50640">helm</a> slot or <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50660">shoulders</a> for example.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51895/deathforged-legplates">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_31.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Deathforged Legplates</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49964/legguards-of-lost-hope">
