<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h3>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a> has potential to be the all-around best mitigation trinket against physical and hybrid damage profiles thanks to its armor and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71578">proc</a> which grants up to +270 stamina at 10 stacks of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71577/invigorated">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_reincarnation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Invigorated</span></a>. However, due the limited 60% proc chance on incoming melee hits and low 10 seconds duration of the buff, stacks may fall unpredictably from a string of avoided attacks, during downtimes due to phase scripts or during tank swaps. As a result, the theoretical maximum EHP granted by the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a> is rarely reached and maintained throughout an entire encounter. That being said, it only takes 3 <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71577/invigorated">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_reincarnation.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Invigorated</span></a> stacks on average throughout the fight to make the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a> the best mitigation trinket against sustained physical damage which makes it an ideal pick for the majority of encounters. <br/>
<br/>On the other hand, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50364/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a> is a more consistent EHP increase in all situations, paired with a phenomenal <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71638">on-use effect</a> increasing resistances to all elements by +268 for 10 seconds, with only a 1-minute cooldown. This on-demand resistance boost on such a short cooldown performs exceptionally well against the deadliest tank-buster abilities of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> such as <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=73061/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a> or <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69409/soul-reaper">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_shadowdance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Reaper</span></a>, which makes <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50364/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a> the best mitigation trinket when it matters most.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50364/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a> + <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a> combo will be your equip-and-forget trinkets for most of the phase once you get them, with a couple of exceptions.<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> remains relevant in Phase 4 as an alternative to the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a> against primarily magic damage, such as <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36855/lady-deathwhisper">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Lady Deathwhisper</span></a> who deals pitiful, inconsistent melee damage as a caster-type AI, <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37972/prince-keleseth">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Prince Keleseth</span></a> who simply does not melee at all, and as the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71510/blood-mirror">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_improvedvampiricembrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Mirror</span></a> tank on <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37955/blood-queen-lanathel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Blood-Queen Lana'thel</span></a> taking 90% shadow and bleed damage. It's also an excellent progression trinket to buffer your HP paired with other defensive cooldowns against deadly tank-buster abilities, far better than the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a> in that regard.<br/>
<br/>Despite having slightly more stamina than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a>, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a> is not that great because its on-use <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71586">6400 absorb</a> can easily be depleted by a melee swing in case of a slight delay in the tank-buster ability you were planning to mitigate with it. On the other hand, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67753/fortitude">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindvision.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fortitude</span></a> will buffer your HP for 15 seconds and provide a better cushion in anticipation of a tank-buster ability and during the recovery after that. The same logic applies to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a>, which will also provide better survival before, during and after a tank-buster ability by reducing the incoming melee attacks that could be fatal following a <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=73061/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a> or<a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69409/soul-reaper">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_shadowdance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Reaper</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>Finally, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47735/glyph-of-indomitability">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Indomitability</span></a> is still a great mitigation trinket against mainly physical damage profiles. While it provides less EHP than the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a>, its <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67694">20-second on-use</a> is far superior to mitigate dangerous burst windows against the likes of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37813/deathbringer-saurfang">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer Saurfang</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=72737/frenzy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_deathpact.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frenzy</span></a> or <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36626/festergut">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Festergut</span></a>'s <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69166/inhaled-blight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_festergutrotface.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inhaled Blight</span></a> x3.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50349/corpse-tongue-coin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_coin_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corpse Tongue Coin</span></a> simply sucks. But can have niche usage if you like solo-ing dungeons as <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=46860/unrelenting-assault">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_unrelentingassault.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unrelenting Assault</span></a> spec.<div class="pad"></div>
