<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons and Shields for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h2>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="main-hand">One-Handed Weapons for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h3>The ilvl 284 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50738/mithrios-bronzebeards-legacy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_117.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mithrios, Bronzebeard's Legacy</span></a> and ilvl 271 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51947/troggbane-axe-of-the-frostborne-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Troggbane, Axe of the Frostborne King</span></a> and are neck and neck at the top for Phase 4 weapons. Their mitigation scores are basically identical, with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51947/troggbane-axe-of-the-frostborne-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Troggbane, Axe of the Frostborne King</span></a> having a combo of defense/<wbr/>dodge/<wbr/>parry secondary stats (107 total), while <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50738/mithrios-bronzebeards-legacy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_117.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mithrios, Bronzebeard's Legacy</span></a>, with its superior item budget, grants just as much avoidance with only defense/<wbr/>parry combined (104 total). However, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50738/mithrios-bronzebeards-legacy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_117.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mithrios, Bronzebeard's Legacy</span></a> takes a slight lead in the threat department thanks to its expertise rating and overall superior DPS.<br/>While they perform identically in DTPS, TMI, and probability of death metrics, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50738/mithrios-bronzebeards-legacy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_117.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mithrios, Bronzebeard's Legacy</span></a> provides a 3.5% TPS increase over the ilvl 271 axe for <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="race" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/human">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_human_male.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Human</span></a>s and <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="race" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/dwarf">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_dwarf_male.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dwarf</span></a> thanks to their <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59224/mace-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_hammer_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mace Specialization</span></a> racial and a 2.6% TPS increase for other races without weapon type preferences. Even <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="race" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/orc">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_orc_male.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Orc</span></a>s and their <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=20574/axe-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Axe Specialization</span></a> racial will see a minor 1% TPS increase over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51947/troggbane-axe-of-the-frostborne-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Troggbane, Axe of the Frostborne King</span></a> due to the expertise rating making up for their racial.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50708/last-word">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_114.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Last Word</span></a> is an interesting weapon with a unique <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71873">proc</a> granting the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71872/blessing-of-light">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_prayerofhealing02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blessing of Light</span></a> buff, which increases your strength by 115 and increases healing received as if the caster of each healing spell had 340 more spell power. The <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71872/blessing-of-light">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_prayerofhealing02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blessing of Light</span></a> buff reaches close to 100% uptime in simulations and increases incoming healing by 1-3%, which doesn't entirely make up for the total lack of secondary stats when it comes to damage mitigation and death probabilities, ranking just below the ilvl 271 version <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49997/mithrios-bronzebeards-legacy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_117.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mithrios, Bronzebeard's Legacy</span></a>. That being said, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50708/last-word">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_114.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Last Word</span></a> can be the best tank weapon in niche situations, such as tanking <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37972/prince-keleseth">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Prince Keleseth</span></a> who does not melee, or as the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=71510/blood-mirror">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_improvedvampiricembrace.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Mirror</span></a> tank on <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37955/blood-queen-lanathel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Blood-Queen Lana'thel</span></a> where no damage can be avoided. Although completely unnecessary, it's a fun weapon swap to have if you want to min-max these roles!<br/>
<br/>Next, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51869/the-facelifter">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_154.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Facelifter</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51937/bonebreaker-scepter">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_117.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bonebreaker Scepter</span></a> perform identically to the ilvl 271 version of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49997/mithrios-bronzebeards-legacy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_117.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mithrios, Bronzebeard's Legacy</span></a> in damage mitigation but, once again, the superior ilvl 271 weapon has a slight edge on threat due to its higher DPS. Both are essentially sidegrades to Phase 3 BiS <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47506/silverwing-defender">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_145.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Silverwing Defender</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47967/crusaders-glory">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_145.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader's Glory</span></a>, with similar mitigation performances but a small 1.5% TPS increase due to their higher DPS. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=46860/unrelenting-assault">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_unrelentingassault.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unrelenting Assault</span></a> enthusiasts can rejoice since Phase 4 finally brings an axe with tank stats that no DPS will contest in the form of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51947/troggbane-axe-of-the-frostborne-king">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Troggbane, Axe of the Frostborne King</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchants</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59619/enchant-weapon-accuracy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Accuracy</span></a> (Threat), <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64579/enchant-weapon-blood-draining">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_note_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Blood Draining</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=27984/enchant-weapon-mongoose">
