<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="shield">Shields for Protection Warrior Tank in Phase 4</h3>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50729/icecrown-glacial-wall">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_75.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Glacial Wall</span></a> is the only ilvl 277 shield in Phase 4 and the default best, while its ilvl 264 version <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50065/icecrown-glacial-wall">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_75.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Glacial Wall</span></a> is the second best. The block value on this shield is just what we need to get slightly above the block soft-cap, which is the only reason why it's the best pick against the only other shield in Phase 4, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=51909/neverending-winter">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_73.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Neverending Winter</span></a>, with less desirable block rating against the heavy hitters of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>.<ul>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<i>You may have noticed that none of the tank items in Phase 4 have block value, except for shields. This is an intentional change from Blizzard to reduce the number of tank items overall and make more of them useable by all tanks, including <a class="icontiny c6" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/death-knight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>
<span class="c6">s</span> who can not block. However, since strength gives block value at a rate of 2 Str = 1 SBV and the higher item level tank gear has a lot of it, the base strength of a full ilvl 277 set plus shield brings us just above the shield block soft-cap. As a result, any more shield block value would be less desirable. In exchange, we got a lot more plate items with bonus armor which turns out to be the most desirable secondary stat for <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>.</i></div></li></ul>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-question">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>
<a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=34009/enchant-shield-major-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_note_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Shield - Major Stamina</span></a> vs <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44936/titanium-plating">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_19.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Titanium Plating</span></a>?</b>
<br/>
<i>As a consequence of less block-oriented items in Phase 4, reaching the block soft-cap with base strength, bosses hitting much harder, and overall split damage profiles, block rating and block value are greatly depreciated in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a>. The advantage of <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44936/titanium-plating">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_19.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Titanium Plating</span></a> over <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=34009/enchant-shield-major-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_note_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Shield - Major Stamina</span></a> earlier in the expansion is gone and both enchants are equal, with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=34009/enchant-shield-major-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_note_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Shield - Major Stamina</span></a> having a slight advantage in survivability, especially against tank-buster abilities, while <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44936/titanium-plating">
